  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $T$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $T$ where every element of $T$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{2,4,6},{8},{10}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${\u2205,{2,4},{6,8},{10}}$ is not a partition because the subset $\u2205$ is empty.\n\n- ${\u2205,{2,4},{6,8},{8,10}}$ is not a partition because the subset $\u2205$ is empty.\n\n- ${{2},{4},{6,8}}$ is not a partition because the element $10\\in T$ does not appear in any subset.\n\n- ${{2},{2,4},{6,8,10}}$ is not a partition because the element $2$ appears in two subsets.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
